== A. Pure Quantitative & Logic

=== C1 \[Hard\] Three Thousand Apples \/ 三千个苹果
*中文：* A、B 两城相距 1000 英里。A 城有 3000 个苹果，卡车最多载 1000 个；只要车上有苹果，每行驶 1 英里司机就吃掉 1 个。允许中途卸货和往返搬运。最多能把多少苹果送到 B？

*English:* Cities A and B are 1,000 miles apart. You have 3,000 apples, a truck capacity of 1,000, and the driver consumes one apple per mile whenever carrying apples. Intermediate caches and return trips are allowed. What is the maximum delivery?

~~~
{}{raw}
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>While more than 2,000 apples remain, three forward loads and two return trips are needed per mile, costing five apples per mile. Move 200 miles to reduce 3,000 to 2,000. With two loads, the cost is three apples per mile; move another $1000/3$ miles to reduce 2,000 to 1,000. The last load then travels the remaining $1000-200-1000/3=1400/3$ miles. The continuous idealization delivers</p><p class="equation-line">$$1000-\frac{1400}{3}=\frac{1600}{3}=533\frac13.$$</p><p>If apples and mile-by-mile consumption must be integral, the deliverable whole-apple count is 533.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== C2 \[Core\] One Hundred Light Bulbs \/ 一百盏灯
*中文：* 100 盏灯初始关闭。第 $k$ 个人切换所有编号为 $k$ 的倍数的灯。100 人依次操作后，哪些灯亮着？

*English:* One hundred bulbs start off. Person $k$ toggles every bulb whose number is a multiple of $k$. Which bulbs remain on after all 100 people act?

~~~
{}{raw}
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>Bulb $n$ is toggled once for each divisor of $n$. Divisors pair as $d$ and $n/d$, except when $n$ is a perfect square. Thus exactly the squares have an odd number of divisors. The illuminated bulbs are</p><p class="equation-line">$$1,4,9,16,25,36,49,64,81,100.$$</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== C3 \[Core\] The Race to Fifty \/ 报数到 50
*中文：* 两人轮流报递增整数。首位玩家可报 1 至 10；之后每个数必须比前一个大 1 至 10。先报出 50 者胜。你是否应先手？策略是什么？

*English:* Players alternately call increasing integers. The first call is from 1 to 10; each later call must exceed the previous by 1 through 10. The first to call 50 wins. Should you move first, and what is the strategy?

~~~
{}{raw}
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>Move first and call <strong>6</strong>. Thereafter, if the opponent increases by $d\in\{1,\ldots,10\}$, increase by $11-d$. Your calls are $6,17,28,39,50$. Each pair of increments totals 11, so the opponent cannot avoid handing you the next target.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== C4 \[Core\] Ants on a Ruler \/ 尺子上的蚂蚁
*中文：* 许多蚂蚁随机落在 100 厘米长的尺子上，以 1 厘米每秒向左或向右直行；迎面相撞时两只都立即掉头。多久后可以保证全部离开尺子？

*English:* Many ants occupy a 100-cm ruler, each moving left or right at 1 cm/s. When two collide head-on, both instantly reverse. How long guarantees that all ants have left?

~~~
{}{raw}
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>For indistinguishable ants, a collision followed by reversal is equivalent to the ants passing through each other and exchanging identities. Every trajectory is therefore a straight path to an endpoint, of length at most 100 cm. The sharp guarantee is <strong>100 seconds</strong>.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== C5 \[Core\] Eight Balls and a Balance \/ 八球找重球
*中文：* 8 个外观相同的球中有 1 个较重。只有一架无砝码天平。如何在两次称量内找出重球？

*English:* One of eight identical-looking balls is heavier. Using a balance scale without weights, identify it in at most two weighings.

~~~
{}{raw}
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>Weigh three balls against three. If they balance, the heavy ball is among the remaining two; weigh them. If they do not balance, it is among the three on the heavier side; weigh two of those against each other. A tilt identifies the heavier one, while balance identifies the third.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== C6 \[Core\] Two Uneven Fuses \/ 两根不均匀导火索
*中文：* 两根导火索各自从一端烧完都恰需 60 分钟，但燃烧速度沿长度不均匀。只有火柴，没有钟。如何量出 45 分钟？

*English:* Each of two nonuniform fuses takes exactly 60 minutes to burn from one end. With matches but no clock, how can you measure 45 minutes?

~~~
{}{raw}
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>At time zero, light both ends of fuse A and one end of fuse B. Fuse A finishes after 30 minutes. At that instant light the other end of B. The remaining portion of B, which would have taken 30 minutes from one end, now burns from both ends in 15 minutes. Total elapsed time: <strong>45 minutes</strong>.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

