== C. Financial Economics

=== C13 \[Core\] Forward Rate from Spot Rates \/ 由即期利率求远期利率
*中文：* 年复利 5 年与 10 年即期利率分别为 10\% 和 15\%。5 年后开始、期限 5 年的远期年化利率是多少？

*English:* With annual compounding, the five-year and ten-year spot rates are 10\% and 15\%. What is the annualized five-year forward rate beginning in year five?

~~~
{}{raw}
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>No arbitrage equates a ten-year investment with a five-year investment rolled into the forward:</p><p class="equation-line">$$ (1.15)^{10}=(1.10)^5(1+f_{5,10})^5.$$</p><p>Therefore</p><p class="equation-line">$$f_{5,10}=\left(\frac{1.15^{10}}{1.10^5}\right)^{1/5}-1\approx0.2023.$$</p><p>The forward rate is approximately <strong>20.23%</strong>. The numerical answer changes with the compounding convention, which must be stated.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== C14 \[Core\] Why Bond Prices Are Convex \/ 债券价格为何凸
*中文：* 画出普通无期权债券价格关于到期收益率的形状，并从现金流贴现公式解释其单调性与凸性。

*English:* Describe the price–yield curve of an option-free bond and explain its monotonicity and convexity from the discounted-cash-flow formula.

~~~
{}{raw}
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>For annual cash flows $CF_t\ge0$,</p><p class="equation-line">$$P(y)=\sum_t\frac{CF_t}{(1+y)^t}.$$</p><p>For admissible $y$, each term has a negative first derivative and positive second derivative, so price decreases with yield and bends upward. Convexity means an equal yield decline produces a larger gain than the loss from an equal yield increase, locally. Embedded options can materially alter this shape.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== C15 \[Medium\] GARCH(1,1) \/ 条件波动率模型
*中文：* 写出 GARCH(1,1) 的基本方程，解释各项，并给出有限无条件方差的典型条件。

*English:* Write the basic GARCH(1,1) equations, interpret the terms, and state the usual condition for a finite unconditional variance.

~~~
{}{raw}
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>A standard specification is</p><p class="equation-line">$$r_t=\mu+\varepsilon_t,\qquad \varepsilon_t=\sigma_t z_t,\qquad \sigma_t^2=\omega+\alpha\varepsilon_{t-1}^2+\beta\sigma_{t-1}^2,$$</p><p>with $\omega&gt;0$, $\alpha,\beta\ge0$, and standardized $z_t$. The shock term reacts to recent squared innovations and the lagged variance term creates persistence. If $\alpha+\beta&lt;1$, the covariance-stationary variance is $\omega/(1-\alpha-\beta)$ under standard assumptions.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

